user_prompt:
Propose 3-5 strong candidate moves for {{side-to-move}} from the position below. Use the supplied analysis as useful context, not as authority.

GROUNDED ANALYSIS:
{{analysis}}

EXCLUDED MOVES:
{{excluded-moves}}{{#if wrong-move}}

ENGINE-REJECTED MOVES:
{{wrong-move}}
These moves must not appear among the candidates.{{/if}}{{#if classic}}

ORTHODOX CHESS POSITION
FEN: {{fen}}

ASCII BOARD:
{{ascii}}{{#if last-move}}

LAST MOVE: {{last-move}}{{/if}}

Use orthodox chess rules, including castling, en passant, promotion, and king safety.{{else}}

VARIANT RULES:
{{chess-rules}}

CURRENT POSITION:
{{board-state}}{{#if last-move}}

LAST MOVE: {{last-move}}{{/if}}{{/if}}

{{#if classic}}The candidate move field must contain one canonical SAN string, including required capture, disambiguation, promotion, and check/checkmate suffixes.{{/if}}{{#if output-uci}}The candidate move field must contain a canonical UCI string: source followed by destination and a lowercase promotion suffix when required.{{/if}}{{#if output-numeric-json}}The candidate move field must be a JSON object with exactly from, to, promotion: {"from":[x,y],"to":[x,y],"promotion":null}. Coordinates are absolute integers; promotion is null or the exact promoted piece name from the legend.{{/if}}{{#if output-semantic}}The candidate move field must be a string: <Color> <PieceName> <from>-<to>. Color is White or Black; use exact piece names and algebraic squares. Captures replace - with x; promotion appends =<PromotionPiece>. Special moves append exactly ' (en-passant)', ' (initial king jump)', or ' (castling; Rook <rook-from>-<rook-to>)'. Use the moving piece identity before the move.{{/if}}{{#if output-numeric}}The candidate move field must be a string: <Color> <PieceName>: (x,y) -> (x,y). Use White or Black, exact piece names, absolute integers, and no spaces within coordinates. Captures replace ' -> ' with ' x '; promotion appends ' = <PromotionPiece>'. Special moves append exactly ' (en-passant)', ' (initial king jump)', or ' (castling; Rook (x,y) -> (x,y))'. Use the moving piece identity before the move.{{/if}}
{{#if numeric-coordinates}}The candidate from and to fields must be absolute 1-based integer arrays [x,y], never mirrored.{{else}}The candidate from and to fields must be absolute algebraic square strings.{{/if}}
